Band Description: The Cathode Cult is less a band and more a collective performance entity, centered around the enigmatic "Mama Data," a figure often obscured by a cascade of glowing fibre optics and repurposed LED screens. Mama Data presides over a hulking, rust-encrusted Hammond B-3, its draws mangled into alien configurations, coaxing spectral groans and soaring laments from its aged pipes. Behind her, the "Ghostgrid Drummers" — a pair of percussionists known only as Hex and Bit — orchestrate a maelstrom of industrial clatter and precise polyrhythms on custom "Arcade Sputter-Drums" fashioned from vintage coin-ops and motherboards. Their masked figures, cloaked in robes woven from old ethernet cables and faded arcade marquees, also operate the "Ghost-Vox Modulator," delivering mournful, processed incantations that hover between human voice and machine cry, crafting towering sonic rituals within the skeletal remains of forgotten shopping centres. Their live performances are less concerts and more spiritual seances for departed algorithms.
